  "invariants": [
    "A candidate below the authoritative revocation floor is denied before authorization is considered; Owner approval cannot override the floor.",
    "A candidate below current epoch but not below the revocation floor requires a valid, scoped, fresh, unrevoked, one-time Owner approval.",
    "The Owner approval resource binds a canonical digest of current/candidate epochs and artifact digests, revocation floor and revision, policy version, and explicit rollback reason.",
    "Current and candidate artifact digests are recomputed using SHA-256 over RFC 8785 JCS canonical bytes.",
    "Provenance and version-bound evidence must each authenticate exactly current_state, candidate_state, revocation_floor and policy_version; each proof is bound to the exact digest, epoch and revision.",
    "Evidence verification must enforce trusted issuer/key, signature, validity, replay resistance, revocation and monotonic revocation-floor revision.",
    "On denial, effective state remains the verified current state; if current state cannot be verified, effective state is unresolved and no digest/epoch is asserted.",
    "Allow and deny output fields are mutually consistent; guard_digest commits to the canonical versioned decision envelope.",
    "Each evidence subject is bound to an explicit subject-specific issuer allowlist; a globally trusted key alone cannot issue every evidence type."
  ],
